Risks / open questions
----------------------
- Sentence-splitting fidelity: a naive splitter can break on "Mr.", "U.S.",
  "3.14", initials ("J. R. R. Tolkien"), etc. Mitigation: split only on
  terminal punctuation + whitespace + a following capital/quote/open-paren;
  never split inside a known abbreviation; and run the splitter AFTER
  `Normalizer` (which already rewrites years/decimal ranges and may defuse some
  decimals). Blast radius of a bad split is only a slightly different pause, not
  lost text.
- More `synthesizeToFile` calls during priming: each call has per-warm-up
  overhead (ticket 02). Priming is transient and uses only a few small chunks,
  so the penalty is bounded and one-time per start; steady state is unchanged.
- Chunk-duration vs. fixed-count look-ahead horizon (see #3).
- `engine.maxSpeechInputLength` must be enforced per chunk regardless of ramp.

