2. Ramp scope (a) first-paragraph-only vs (b) until-buffer-primed
   (recommended)?
3. Always-on vs. a user toggle (default on)?
4. Treat title/heading as its own single chunk at cold start (recommended)?
==Status Report: 2026-10-17 (IMPLEMENTED)==

User said "go" without answering the four decision points, so I took the plan's
recommendations and left ticket 25 alone as requested:
1. Ramp ladder: 1, 2, 4, rest-of-paragraph.
2. Ramp scope: the first PRIME_PARAGRAPHS (3) paragraphs from any fresh start,
   approximating "until the look-ahead buffer is primed".
3. A user toggle (default ON) — the "option" in the ticket filename.
4. Title/heading stays a single chunk at cold start.

Implemented:
- `tts/SpeechController.kt`
  - Added private `Chunk(utteranceIndex, text, isFirstOfParagraph)` and moved the
    synthesis/play-back/play-head/look-ahead pipeline onto a `chunks` list, while
    `queue` remains the paragraph-level tracking list.
  - `buildChunks()`: title/heading = one chunk; the first 3 paragraphs from a
    (re)start use the sentence ladder (1, 2, 4, rest); later paragraphs are whole
    chunks. Runs on normalized text; chunks are capped at
    `TextToSpeech.getMaxSpeechInputLength()` via `splitToFit`.
  - `onUtteranceStarted` now fires only for `Chunk.isFirstOfParagraph`, so the
    blue line / bookmarks stay paragraph-level (MainViewModel unchanged).
  - `enqueueFrom` / `skipSections` / `resume` map chunk -> owning utterance.
  - Look-ahead horizon re-expressed in chunk units (`LOOK_AHEAD_CHUNKS = 8`).
- `SettingsStore.kt` — `progressiveChunking` (default true).
- `SettingsActivity.kt` — "Sentence-by-sentence start" toggle under Playback.

Validation: `compileDebugKotlin`, `testDebugUnitTest`, and `assembleDebug` all
